{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 12, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a 2010 american biographical drama film directed by david fincher and written by jesse eisenberg. the film is based on the book \"the accidental billionaire\" by ben mezrich, which tells the story of the founding of the social networking site facebook.\n\nthe film stars jesse eisenberg as mark zuckerberg, the co-founder and former ceo of facebook. the movie also features a talented cast, including andrew garfield as eduardo saverin, justin timberlake as sean parker, and armie hammer as the winklevoss twins.\n\nthe story begins at harvard university, where mark zuckerberg is a sophomore and a computer science major. he creates a website called \"facemash\" which becomes a huge hit on campus, but also gets him into trouble with the university administration. this experience sparks an idea in mark's mind, and he begins to work on a new project called facebook.\n\nmark's initial idea for facebook is to create a website that allows users to create their own profiles and connect with their friends. however, as the site grows in popularity, mark's vision for facebook begins to change. he becomes more interested in creating a website that can be used by the entire harvard student body, and eventually, the entire world.\n\nmeanwhile, a group of students, including the winklevoss twins, are working on their own social networking site called \"connectu\". they claim that mark has stolen their idea and are determined to take him down. the film explores the complex and often contentious relationship between mark and the winklevoss twins, as well as the rivalry between mark and sean parker, who is also working on a social networking site.\n\nthe film features a range of themes, including the consequences of ambition, the importance of friendship and loyalty, and the impact of technology on our lives. it also raises questions about the ethics of innovation and the responsibilities that come with creating something that can have a huge impact on people's lives.\n\nthe film's performances are outstanding, with jesse eisenberg delivering a particularly impressive performance as mark zuckerberg. andrew garfield is also excellent as eduardo saverin, bringing a sense of vulnerability and sensitivity to the character. justin timberlake is great as sean parker, capturing the charismatic and confident personality of the character.\n\nthe film's direction is also noteworthy, with david fincher using a range of techniques to create a sense of tension and unease. the film's score, composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is also excellent, capturing the mood and atmosphere of the film perfectly.\n\noverall, the social network is a gripping and thought-provoking film that explores the complexities of the tech industry and the impact of technology on our lives. it is a must-see for anyone interested in the story of facebook and the people who created it.\n\nrating: 9/10\n\nduration: 120 minutes\n\ngenre: drama, biography\n\nrelease date: october 1, 2010\n\ndirected by: david fincher\n\nwritten by: jesse eisenberg\n\nstarring: jesse eisenberg, andrew garfield, justin timberlake, armie hammer, joshua jackson, ralph finnes, max minghella, and eduardo rodrigues.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.045232724}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.0016868184}, {"token": " network", "logprob": -7.6293654e-06}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.18040486}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.00012385078}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.32515162}, {"token": "201", "logprob": -2.9086643e-05}, {"token": "0", "logprob": -3.933899e-06}, {"token": " american", "logprob": -0.3342006}, {"token": " bi", "logprob": -0.0031711787}, {"token": "ographical", "logprob": -0.00043990472}, {"token": " drama", "logprob": -0.011117537}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.00057299406}, {"token": " directed", "logprob": -0.18416922}, {"token": " by", "